{
  "id": "arrays/array-key-for-string-key",
  "title": "An array<array-key, int> argument cannot satisfy a parameter declared array<string, int>",
  "domain": "arrays",
  "criterion_id": "arrays/element-key-type-contract",
  "rule_class": "argument.type",
  "php": { "min": "8.1" },
  "targets": ["src"],
  "source_candidate_id": "psalm:6e0079989da3fbda2530",
  "ground_truth": {
    "basis": "runtime_proof",
    "statement": "An array key is an int or a string and nothing else, and array-key is int|string, so an array declared array<array-key, int> is an array<int|string, int> and may contain int keys - the argument here contains the int key 0. The callee declares array<string, int> and applies strtoupper() to every key, which under strict_types fails with a TypeError on that int key. Passing an argument of type array<array-key, int> into a parameter of type array<string, int> is therefore unsound: the declared key type is a contract the argument cannot meet, and a diagnostic belongs on the call. PHP also normalises a numeric string key to int, so the caller cannot satisfy a string key type by spelling key 0 as '0' either.",
    "runtime_script": "runtime/check.php",
    "citation": "https://www.php.net/manual/en/language.types.array.php"
  },
  "expect": {
    "phpstan": {
      "mode": "unsupported",
      "basis": "upstream_docs",
      "reason": "PHPStan explicitly defines array-key as a permissive benevolent union rather than a strictly checked int|string alias. ArrayType normalizes that key to implicit mixed, and this baseline level-9 configuration leaves checkImplicitMixed disabled. Silence is therefore an excluded documented configuration-scope difference. An independent check with checkImplicitMixed: true emits argument.type on the unchanged fixture; the rule is implemented.",
      "citation": "https://phpstan.org/config-reference#checkbenevolentuniontypes"
    },
    "psalm": {
      "mode": "diagnostics",
      "required": [{ "code": "MixedArgumentTypeCoercion", "line": 26 }]
    },
    "mago": {
      "mode": "diagnostics",
      "required": [{ "code": "less-specific-argument", "line": 26 }]
    }
  },
  "notes": "This tests the array key contract, distinct from the element value contract. The runtime consequence remains real: an int key reaches strtoupper() under strict_types and throws. Psalm 6.20.0 and Mago 1.57.0 diagnose the call. The initial factory report counted PHPStan's level-9 silence as FN, but a later source and documentation audit corrected that classification without changing the fixture or its runtime result. PHPStan's configuration reference explicitly documents array-key as a benevolent union with deliberately lenient checking. In the pinned source, TypeNodeResolver.php:283-284 constructs that union; ArrayType.php:75-82 normalizes it to implicit mixed. The baseline checkImplicitMixed:false then deliberately accepts the key. An independent unchanged-source probe with checkImplicitMixed:true emits argument.type; an explicit int|string spelling also diagnoses. This is a documented dialect/configuration difference, not a missing implemented check, and is excluded consistently with the optional PHPDoc signature check. The older immutable factory reports retain the original FN for audit history; use the corrected cohort report for current claims. The Psalm candidate is a lead only: its suppressed upstream coercion is not the oracle for any tool.",
  "provenance": {
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "catalogue_candidate",
        "id": "psalm:6e0079989da3fbda2530",
        "family": "psalm",
        "provider": "providerValidCodeParse",
        "path": "tests/ArgTest.php",
        "line": 172,
        "source_ref": "62e52cd9fe3ab4429debc0eb0306057419b0a9d6",
        "source_sha256": "5312753663b0002d41083ecc1cd656667c8f2007780efce050c9874a0ba290fb",
        "citation": "https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/blob/62e52cd9fe3ab4429debc0eb0306057419b0a9d6/tests/ArgTest.php#L172",
        "note": "lead only; the explicit int key type on the argument side is the part that is kept, the rule was re-derived from the runtime"
      },
      {
        "kind": "upstream_source",
        "revision": "2c12dac5e4f8626c8a7cfc0b4bb9c5ce48d37c96",
        "citation": "https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2c12dac5e4f8626c8a7cfc0b4bb9c5ce48d37c96/src/PhpDoc/TypeNodeResolver.php#L283-L284",
        "note": "array-key deliberately resolves to a BenevolentUnionType, not a plain int|string union"
      },
      {
        "kind": "upstream_source",
        "revision": "2c12dac5e4f8626c8a7cfc0b4bb9c5ce48d37c96",
        "citation": "https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2c12dac5e4f8626c8a7cfc0b4bb9c5ce48d37c96/src/Type/ArrayType.php#L75-L85",
        "note": "the benevolent int|string key normalizes to implicit mixed; StrictMixedType becomes a checked plain union"
      },
      {
        "kind": "upstream_source",
        "path": "/home/abez/projects/phpstan-src/src/Rules/RuleLevelHelper.php",
        "revision": "2c12dac5e4f8626c8a7cfc0b4bb9c5ce48d37c96",
        "note": "transformCommonType / transformMixedType map a mixed type to StrictMixedType only when checkExplicitMixed (explicit mixed) or checkImplicitMixed (implicit mixed) is on; with both off the type is returned unchanged and an unspecified key stays lenient, which is why the level-9 run is silent here"
      },
      {
        "kind": "upstream_source",
        "path": "/home/abez/projects/phpstan-src/conf/config.neon",
        "revision": "2c12dac5e4f8626c8a7cfc0b4bb9c5ce48d37c96",
        "note": "line 73 sets checkImplicitMixed: false in the default configuration; conf/config.level10.neon line 5 sets it true, and conf/config.levelmax.neon includes config.level10.neon"
      }
    ],
    "tool_pins": { "mago": "1.57.0", "phpstan": "2.3.1", "psalm": "6.20.0" },
    "source_checkouts": {
